      "content": {
        "id": "c0fe0c85-f824-36da-851d-0516a44c6d19",
        "contentType": "STORY",
        "title": "Chinese AI firm MiniMax, others launch Hong Kong IPOs in year-end rush", // 职位
        "description": "",
        "summary": "Chinese AI startup MiniMax Group spearheaded six Hong Kong listings worth HK$16.7 billion ($2.15 billion) launched on Wednesday, exchange ​filings showed, as AI and chipmakers power the city's equity markets comeback and set the tone for 2026. Hong Kong ‌has raised $36.5 billion from 114 new listings in 2025, for its strongest year since 2021, and more than triple the roughly $11.3 billion raised in 2024, LSEG ‌data shows. MiniMax seeks to raise up to HK$4.19 billion from 25.4 million shares priced in a range of HK$151.00 to HK$165.00 each, ahead of a January 9 debut.",
